{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Gamma.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.PSeries","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.balanced_bar_invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.balanced_bar_invariance","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L296-L308","doc":"**The balanced repair (the bar-projection caveat, exact).** In the\ndoubled variable (`q_paper = Q²`, the `BalancedQuantumTwist` convention)\nthe reflection identity reads `[m]_{Q²}! = (Q²)^{C(m,2)}·[m]_{Q⁻²}!` —\nwhich is precisely the statement that the BALANCED normalizer\n`Q^{−C(m,2)}·[m]_{Q²}!` is bar-invariant (`Q ↦ Q⁻¹`): dividing both sides\nby `Q^{C(m,2)}` matches term for term. The identification survives iff the\nconjecture's kernel is read in this balanced convention — matching the\nproper time's reality (bar-invariance), with vanishing first-order\n`q`-correction (probe E3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.keystone_normalizer_not_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.keystone_normalizer_not_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L279-L294","doc":"**The falsifier fires.** If the bar weight is nontrivial\n(`q^{C(m,2)} ≠ 1`) and the reflected factorial is nonzero, the one-sided\nq-factorial is NOT bar-invariant: `[m]_q! ≠ [m]_{q⁻¹}!`. For the keystone\nnormalizer (`m = n−1`) the weight is nontrivial for every `n ≥ 3` at\ngeneric `q ≠ 1` — the unbalanced-kernel identification is refuted at\n`q ≠ 1` (scope-(a): this stated form only). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.qfact_reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.qfact_reflect","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L259-L277","doc":"**Bar reflection of the q-factorial.**\n`[m]_q! = q^{C(m,2)}·[m]_{q⁻¹}!` with `C(m,2) = m(m−1)/2`. Applied to the\nkeystone normalizer `N_q(n) = [n−1]_q!` (`m = n−1`): the binding q-Borel\nnormalizer is bar-COVARIANT with exact weight `q^{C(n−1,2)}` — while the\nloop proper time (`s` real) is bar-INVARIANT. This is the Attack-E\nfalsifier: the identification with the unbalanced kernel fails at `q ≠ 1`\n(scope-(a); at `q = 1` the weight is 1 and the classical identification is\nuntouched). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.qint_reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.qint_reflect","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L243-L257","doc":"**Bar reflection of the one-sided quantum integer.**\n`[k+1]_q = q^k·[k+1]_{q⁻¹}` — the one-sided `[k]_q = 1 + q + … + q^{k−1}`\n(the corpus convention, `QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qint`) is\nbar-covariant with monomial weight. Index stated at `k+1` so the exponent\n`k` is subtraction-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.kernel_moments_eq_schwinger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.kernel_moments_eq_schwinger","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L224-L235","doc":"**The reduction, proved conditionally.** Any kernel satisfying the\nhypothesis class is moment-indistinguishable from the unit Schwinger\nkernel: every `ds/s`-moment agrees. The remaining gap to\n`K_b = e^{−s}` (a.e.) is exactly the classical determinacy step whose\nCarleman hypothesis `carleman_divergence` proves — so the conjecture is\nreduced to the class's two named hypotheses, nothing else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation.moments","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation.moments","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L221-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation.integrable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation.integrable","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L219-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation.positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation.positive","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L218-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L217-L217","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.BindingKernelSchwingerRepresentation","kind":"class","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L195-L222","doc":"**Conjecture carrier (primary; no instance exists or may be created).**\nThe binding Borel resummation kernel — the weight `K_b(s)·ds` realizing the\nkeystone-forced normalizer as `N(n+1) = n! = ∫ s^{n+1}·K_b(s)·ds/s` — is a\npositive measure on `(0,∞)` with exactly the factorial `ds/s`-moments.\nThese fields are the two OPEN hypotheses that Attack A reduces the\nconjecture \"binding Borel variable = loop proper time\" to:\n\n* `positive` + `integrable` — the substrate resummation weight is a genuine\n  positive measure (open: no corpus result establishes it; the C1 carrier\n  coefficients `I(n)/n!` are NOT themselves a Stieltjes moment sequence —\n  log-convexity fails at `m = 2` — so this is a statement about the\n  kernel, not the coefficients);\n* `moments` — its moments are the keystone-forced factorials (open: the\n  keystone forces the NORMALIZER values `(n−1)!`, not that they arise as\n  the moments of the substrate's own kernel).\n\nGiven both, `kernel_moments_eq_schwinger` below (proved) plus classical\nCarleman–Stieltjes determinacy (`carleman_divergence` proves its\nhypothesis; the theorem itself is classical, unformalized) force\n`K_b(s)·ds = e^{−s}·ds` — the identification. Creating an `instance` of\nthis class would launder the conjecture (§Axiomatization is NOT a Proof);\nnone exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.half_unit_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.half_unit_fails","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L184-L190","doc":"**The rival unit `c = ½` is impossible** against the proved keystone\nidentity — the exact `n!/2 ≠ n!` distinguisher, for every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.unit_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.unit_forced","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L165-L182","doc":"**Unit forcing.** With kernel `c·e^{−s}·ds/s` the moments are\n`c·(n−1)!`; the PROVED keystone identity `n·N(n) = n!` (shifted:\n`(n+1)·N(n+1) = (n+1)!` with `N(n+1) = c·n!`) forces `c = 1` exactly.\nConditional on the Borel-variable = proper-time identification, the\nSchwinger measure unit is pinned — the r2core §5 distinguisher. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.carleman_divergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.carleman_divergence","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L147-L163","doc":"**Carleman divergence.** `Σ_k (k!)^{−1/(2k)} = ∞` (stated as\nnon-summability): the Carleman condition for the Stieltjes moment problem\nof `{k!}` HOLDS. By the classical Carleman–Stieltjes determinacy theorem\n(Simon 1998; NOT formalized in Mathlib — this lemma proves its exact\nhypothesis) the problem is determinate: `e^{−s}·ds` is the UNIQUE positive\nmeasure on `(0,∞)` with moments `{k!}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.carleman_minorant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.carleman_minorant","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L114-L145","doc":"**The Carleman minorant.** The Carleman term of the shifted moment\nsequence `{k!}` dominates the harmonic term: `1/k ≤ (k!)^{−1/(2k)}`, from\nthe exact bound `k! ≤ k^{2k}`. This is the quantitative heart of\nCarleman's condition for `{k!}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.moment_eq_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorelProperTimeMoment.moment_eq_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorelProperTimeMoment.lean#L93-L112","doc":"**The moment identity.** The `(n+1)`-st `ds/s`-moment of the unit\n(`c = 1`) Schwinger kernel is exactly `n!`:\n`∫₀^∞ s^{n+1}·e^{−s}·ds/s = Γ(n+1) = n!`. Unshifted this is\n`∫ s^n e^{−s} ds/s = (n−1)!` for `n ≥ 1` — the keystone-forced binding\nnormalizer `N(n) = (n−1)!` (`KeystoneBridgeC1Binding`) IS the moment data\nof the loop's proper-time kernel. Index shifted by 1 so ℕ-arithmetic stays\nsubtraction-free. ","signatureChunk":0}]}